        "notes": "WARN, not pass and not fail. The Lean now states the .md claim faithfully and ASSUMES it: `tannaka_krein_reconstruction` is an `axiom`, declared as such, for a published external result (Woronowicz 1988 Thm 1.1, Deligne 1990 Thm 7.1, Kassel 1995 Thm XI.4.1). An axiom for a cited theorem is a legitimate pattern when it is labelled, and it is; but it does not DERIVE the .md claim, so this is not a pass. WHAT THIS COMMIT FIXED, and it was the serious half. The axiom took `(tau_monoidal : Prop) (tau_faithful : Prop) (tau_exact : Prop)` -- ARGUMENTS OF TYPE Prop, not proofs -- and never mentioned them again. It therefore asserted a Tannaka-Krein reconstruction for EVERY rigid braided monoidal C and every k, while reading as though it required a well-behaved fibre functor: a caller passed True three times and got the conclusion. AGENTS.md 'Axiomatization is NOT a Proof' forbids exactly that shape. They are now the actual functor tau : C -> ModuleCat k with [tau.Faithful], [tau.Monoidal], [PreservesFiniteLimits tau] and [PreservesFiniteColimits tau], all resolved against the pinned Mathlib. The CONCLUSION was vacuous too and is no longer: both `monoidal_equiv` and `universal_property` were Prop-universe fields, so a witness set both to True and the carrier to anything. The equivalence is now DATA, `equiv : C imp RepCat`, so a witness must produce an actual equivalence of categories. WHY WARN AND NOT PASS, precisely: (1) it is assumed, not derived; (2) `universal_property` remains a Prop-universe field and is still chooseable -- terminality quantifies over factorisations through Rep of OTHER Hopf algebras, so encoding it needs the 2-category of Hopf-algebra representation categories, not just one more carried field; (3) the equivalence is of CATEGORIES, not of MONOIDAL categories, since a monoidal structure on the carried RepCat is downstream of the same gap -- the field is named `equiv` rather than `monoidal_equiv` so the name and the type agree. VERIFICATION NOTE, because it is not reproducible on a stock container: this file imports Mathlib.RingTheory.HopfAlgebra.Basic, which is ABSENT from the restored lake-cache olean tree (one of the four gaps AGENTS.md documents), so the file was unverifiable here -- before this change as well as after. Verified by building the missing cone (TensorProduct.Finiteness, Coalgebra.Basic, Bialgebra.Basic, HopfAlgebra.Basic) into a hardlink-overlay shadow and compiling against it: lean -DautoImplicit=false -s 65536 exit 0. The real olean tree was not written to."
      }
